# Scoped deliberately narrowly — NOT `* text=auto`, which would renormalise every tracked file in
# the repo and bury the next real diff.
#
# These are the files the Raspberry Pi consumes directly (see PI-HOSTING-PLAN.md). They are authored
# on Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` normalises CRLF away on commit — but that is a per-clone
# *setting*, not a property of the repo, so a commit made with it unset would ship CRLF and each of
# these fails in its own opaque way: `.env` puts a trailing \r inside the tunnel token (cloudflared
# reports an auth error, not a parse error), and a `.sh` with CRLF dies as
# `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`. Pin the ending instead of depending on the setting.
Dockerfile         text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
Caddyfile          text eol=lf
.env.example       text eol=lf
*.sh               text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the systemd units. systemd does not strip CR: a CRLF unit file gives
# `ExecStart=` a path with a trailing \r, and the unit fails with a "No such file or directory"
# naming a path that visibly exists.
*.service          text eol=lf
*.timer            text eol=lf
